OK, let's set aside offsets and payloads for this issue.

My initial idea in LUCENE-2878 was for nextPosition() to return NO_MORE_POSITIONS (defined as -1) when it's exhausted.  So if you request positions from a Scorer that doesn't support them at all, it can just return NO_MORE_POSITIONS immediately.  Clients know that to iterate through a Scorer's positions, you do:
{code}
int pos;
while ((pos = scorer.nextPosition()) != NO_MORE_POSITIONS) {
  // do stuff
}
{code}
And this way Scorers that don't support positions (or that don't make sense to return them) are dealt with naturally.

{quote}
