Basically, the circle is divided into sectors.  The sector edges must go through the center of the circle and the center of the world.  The potential problems come in because each sector meets the line from the circle center to the center of the world at a different point.  As long as that point is not actually *outside* of the world, though, that is fine, since we're describing a Geo shape that resides on the surface of the world, not underneath.

So I see how this works and I agree that it is an improvement, although I also think we will need to have code that detects when we're building sectors that are illegal.

